# Work lifecycle

Full detail: `AGENTS.md`, section "Work lifecycle". Repository: `APESCIC/NPO.WorkDash`.

Before the first edit:

1. Find the issue (`gh issue list --search "..."`) or create one with a `[Epic]`, `[Story]`, `[Task]`, `[Bug]` or `[Chore]` title prefix, the matching label, area labels, and the usual body sections (Summary, Context / why, Scope, Acceptance criteria, Out of scope, Dependencies).
2. Set its milestone (`gh issue edit <n> --milestone "M0 Foundation"`) and link it under its parent:

   ```powershell
   $id = gh api repos/APESCIC/NPO.WorkDash/issues/<child> --jq '.id'
   gh api -X POST repos/APESCIC/NPO.WorkDash/issues/<parent>/sub_issues -F sub_issue_id=$id
   ```

3. Branch from `main`: `cursor/{feature|fix|chore}/<issue>-<slug>`. Never commit to `main`.

While working:

- Comment on the issue for decisions, blockers, scope changes and when the PR opens.
- Split large work into linked sub-issues instead of growing one issue.
- Tick acceptance criteria as they are met.

When finished:

- Close the leaf issue with a comment linking the PR and release.
- Close a parent only when all its sub-issues are closed.
- Check the milestone's open/closed count.
